<p>I'm upvoting but I agree with the commenters above that the interview did feel too in your face. The Parawatch post already does a good job of showing what the book was about, and I feel like having the author be voiceless adds to the mystery. It feel jarring compared to the containment procedures and the description which do a good job of keeping on that sweet spot between vague and explicit. The table especially does a great job at this. The super minimalist nature of it really sets the mood. I also love the cover image.</p>

