				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ayers" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1856789); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1856789&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200835" alt="Ayers" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1856789)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ayers" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1856789); return false;" >Ayers</a></span> <span class="odate time_1576059418 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Dec 2019 10:16</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4443239">
									

<p>Due to overwhelming public consensus, I've gone ahead and removed the interview section of this article. Personally, I thought it was <em>too</em> ambiguous, but I guess I kinda forced my interpretation of the article in the dialogue which, ironically, is against what I was trying to do with this whole thing. Sometimes you have to kill your darlings, I guess.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;bigger&nbsp;reasons&nbsp;with&nbsp;spoilers&nbsp;and&nbsp;authorial&nbsp;intent</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[–]&nbsp;cool</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The interview was, I suppose, me trying to nudge the reader towards the symbolic side of things, where Masquerade acts kind of ideological &quot;self-help&quot; mechanisms that are simultaneously self-destructive but also, in the short-term, helpful. I had solipsism in mind when writing this, but I suppose the metaphor works for these in general. The way I did this was dry and without subtext, which understandably made the interview feel overly-expository &#8212; that said, I also feel that without the interview, this may be too undetectable.</p>
<p>At the same time, I felt I also had to nudge the reader towards the physical side of things, which made it a bit of an incoherent, confused mess. Kids *are* going missing, and they are being used to fuel new editions &#8212; but that's not what Clyde was talking about 3 sentences ago.</p>
<p>The main mechanical purpose of the interview, though, was to make the reader question why Masquerade is collecting masks so her actions are scrutinised a little bit more and not just disregarded as &quot;spooky storytelling&quot;.</p>
<p>Anyway, that's why I thought the interview was a good idea and, in hindsight, probably wasn't.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

